WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.834
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.282
- All right, y'all, it's the holidays,

00:00:02.282 --> 00:00:04.290
and we've picked out something
perfect for the season.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.661
Trending on social media,
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.661 --> 00:00:07.870
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.076
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.980
- You all know I'm a sucker

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.170
for a well-decorated Christmas tree,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.610
really any Christmas tree.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.660
I love Christmas.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.910
But getting the lights
and ornaments just right

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.260
can take some serious work,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.180
especially if you're not
smart and buy pre-lit.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.170
Whatever.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.170
That's why I love this hack
an Alabama man came up with

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.578
after and while enjoying a little wine.

00:00:28.578 --> 00:00:31.578
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:35.997 --> 00:00:37.291
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:39.230
- That's a resourceful
man, I'm just saying.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.090
We have this master inventor
on the line right now

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.970
watching on WVTM 13 in Birmingham.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.382
What's up, Mike?

00:00:46.382 --> 00:00:48.026
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:48.026 --> 00:00:50.700
- Hello, Kelly. (laughing)

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.533
- [Kelly] All right.

00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:53.100
So, Mike, you gotta set
up this scene for us.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.030
So you didn't have a ladder.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.370
That was a very clever thing you did.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.130
- No, actually, the way
it started out was...

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.750
Of course, it's a wonderful time,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.970
to have Christmas and put the tree up.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.060
But this time the wife
bought a different tree

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.700
and she brought in two boxes

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.600
and I thought, "What the hell?"

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.720
You know, "This is a
construction site now.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.240
It's not just taking it out of the box

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.440
and setting it on the coffee table

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.120
and putting a bulb on it."

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.060
So, yeah, I got the stepladder

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.300
and I got ready to put the lights on it,

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.030
turned around, she's walking
away with the stepladder,

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.640
said I had way too much wine already.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.130
So I had to think fast and
that's where the broom came in.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:33.963
- It was so clever.

00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:36.690
And you are so welcome on
this show, anytime, man.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.726
Your accent is... I'm loving it.

00:01:38.726 --> 00:01:40.458
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:01:40.458 --> 00:01:41.960
And you are so funny.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.950
So this kind of... this blew up.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.930
This made you famous in town, right?

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:46.770
- [Mike] Oh yeah, yeah.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.960
Of course, I live in a little town.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.290
I shared it with the
people at work, my friends,

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.550
the people I hang out with,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.500
and, well, within no time

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.090
they're spreading that
(beep) around everywhere.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.337
So that's (voice drowned out)

00:01:59.337 --> 00:02:02.072
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:02.072 --> 00:02:04.518
- I would love to hang out with you.

00:02:04.518 --> 00:02:05.790
(Kelly, audience and Mike laughing)

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.860
You are a bit like a member of my family.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.160
It is insane how we are similar.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.220
Thank you so much, Mike, for
the innovative, creative idea.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.260
That was a very smart thing
to do with that broom.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.060
Because it's the perfect
bristles, you know, to go through.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.350
That was very smart.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.090
- Oh yeah.
- Thank you for sharing.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.680
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.690
- I'm liking your post right now, Mike.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:25.947
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:25.947 --> 00:02:27.960
And I'm loving you.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:28.793
That's not all.

00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:31.890
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of Precise,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.480
the go-to pen of The Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.360
want to honor truly,
truly incredible people,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.193
just like you.

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:39.550
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.432
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:41.432 --> 00:02:42.768
- Oh, that's great. Thank you.

00:02:42.768 --> 00:02:43.601
- [Kelly] Thanks Mike.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.850
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.375
Cher, Laila Lockhart
Kraner, Big Time Rush,

00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:50.388
(voice drowned out).

00:02:50.388 --> 00:02:52.008
And on the Day of the Elf,
you all have a great day.

00:02:52.008 --> 00:02:53.758
And if it's not, try and change it.

